From a362b48cbfb69921b7ff63971944a635d3f2af66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:33:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CEC: the settings of an adapter on another output say the
 remote does not reach Kodi

A CEC adapter on another output than Kodi's picture (an AV receiver on
the HDMI port of the board while the picture goes to the TV from a
graphics card) cannot bring the TV's remote to Kodi: the TV sends its
keys to the device on the input that is watched. Kodi only said so in
kodi.log ("CEC: the adapter ... is on ..., and Kodi's picture is on
..."), and the user saw a remote that does nothing (issue #24).

The settings of such an adapter (Settings > System > Input > Peripherals)
now begin with a line "TV remote: not through this adapter"; a press of
it says on which output each one is (the names of the DRM connectors,
from sysfs), why the keys do not come, how to have them (the picture
from the output that has CEC, or a USB CEC adapter on the cable of the
picture) and that a receiver wired so on purpose needs no change. It is
said there, where one looks when the remote does nothing, and nowhere
else: no notice at a start, since it may be wired so on purpose. The
line is there only while the adapter is on another output
(CPeripheral::GetSettingsNote()).

New strings #62340 and #62341, translated in Estuary (#54340, #54341:
es_es, es_ar, es_mx).
